{"term":"halt","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:a7c631fab899032c18","definition":"To limp; move with a limping gait.","example":"Here comes Sir Toby halting — you shall hear more; but if he had not been in drink, he would have tickled you othergates than he did.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"intransitive, obsolete","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/halt#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:933b902f3021541494","definition":"To stand in doubt whether to proceed, or what to do; hesitate; be uncertain; linger; delay; mammer.","example":"How long halt ye between two opinions?","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"intransitive, obsolete","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/halt#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f63e95a15410c79811","definition":"To be lame, faulty, or defective, as in connection with ideas, or in measure, or in versification.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"intransitive, obsolete","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/halt#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8b1cad0fd93c57a8b8","definition":"To waver.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/halt#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:48c426bf79dab944db","definition":"To falter.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[